# CONTRIBUTING

In order to extend this library, we must follow some rules;

This document outlines the rules, workflows, and standards required to
maintain the library's high-performance, zero-copy, and FFI-first
architecture.

## Core Principles

iolating these will result in immediate rejection of your contribution.

1. Pure C99. No C++, no C++ exceptions, no C++ templates.
   The ABI must remain stable for C, C++, Python, and Lua.

2. Zero-Copy Hot Path. execute() function of any DSP block must never call 
   malloc, free, realloc, or any other memory allocation function. 
   Memory is allocated once in create() and freed in destroy().
   
3. Explicit FFI: All functions must return only scalar types 
   rflib_status_t, size_t, float). Data flows via pointer arguments with
   explicit length parameters. No variadic functions (...) are allowed.

## Getting Started

#### Prerequisites

    Compiler: GCC 9+, Clang 10+, or MSVC 2019+ (C99 mode).
    Build System: CMake 3.14+.
    Language: C99 (strictly).
    Testing: Python 3.9+ (with numpy, cffi) and LuaJIT 2.1+ (optional but
    recommended for FFI testing).
    Reference Tools: SciPy (for filter validation), Valgrind (Linux), 
    AddressSanitizer (all platforms).

## Environment Setup

```bash

# Clone the repository
$ git clone https://github.com/nflatrea/rflib.git
$ cd rflib

# Create build directory
$ mkdir build && cd build

# Configure (Monolithic build)
$ cmake -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug -DRFLIB_BUILD_TESTS=ON ..

# Build
$ cmake --build . -j$(nproc)

```
